# component: alert-dialog
# decisions: A11Y-9, BRD-1, DOC-1, DOC-2, OVL-13
# hunks:
#   OVL-13: `AlertDialogPortal` reads `useInternalThemeScope()` and wraps its children in a
#     `display: contents` element carrying that class — the same host shape `dialog` uses.
#   A11Y-9: `AlertDialogContent` mirrors Base UI's `data-base-ui-inert` markers onto native
#     `inert` through `useModalInert`. No `modal` context here: Base UI's AlertDialog OMITS the
#     `modal` prop from its root (`Omit<DialogRoot.Props, 'modal' | …>`), so an alert dialog is
#     always modal and the hook is always enabled.
#   BRD-1: `AlertDialogContent` draws a real 1px `border border-border` instead of upstream's
#     `ring-1 ring-foreground/10` box-shadow outline (MK reversed BRD-1 to ours, 23-09-2026). A
#     border survives forced colours and matches `foundations/elevation`; nothing else moves.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: prettier reflow plus the `registry-stamp.mjs` provenance header (DOC-1); no
#               decision of their own.
